{"conversation":"I think I can try to keep two arrays or lists for max scores: one for when I ended on an even number and one for when I ended on an odd number. Then I can update these arrays when I go through nums.","python_code":"class Solution:
    def maxScore(self, nums: List[int], x: int) -> int:
        n = len(nums)
        max_even = [float('-inf')] * n
        max_odd = [float('-inf')] * n
        # Initialize the start
        if nums[0] % 2 == 0:
            max_even[0] = nums[0]
        else:
            max_odd[0] = nums[0]

        for i in range(1, n):
            num = nums[i]
            if num % 2 == 0:
                # If current num is even, take max of coming from even or odd
                max_even[i] = max(max_even[i-1] + num, max_odd[i-1] + num - x)
                max_odd[i] = max_odd[i-1]  # no update when current is even for odd array
            else:
                # If current num is odd
                max_odd[i] = max(max_odd[i-1] + num, max_even[i-1] + num - x)
                max_even[i] = max_even[i-1]  # no update when current is odd for even array

        return max(max_even[-1], max_odd[-1])"}
